{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation and configuration evidence map for the provisional candidates.\\n\\n- Operation certificates. src/rebar/schemas/sign_result.schema.json and docs/migrations/hmac-opcert-removal.md establish sshsig over a DSSE envelope for plan-review and completion-verifier certificates. The maintained HMAC claims listed in the prior checkpoint conflict with that contract.\\n- Ticket relations. docs/ticket-model.md and src/rebar/_cli/help/unlink.txt establish seven relations, including caused_by, and an optional relation selector for unlink. README.md and client templates conflict.\\n- Claim identity. docs/config.md and docs/user-guide.md establish configured default assignment and Jira-resolvable explicit identities. README.md, client templates, the demo SVG, and .agents/rules/rebar.md instruct explicit placeholder or bare-handle assignment.\\n- Import behavior. src/rebar/_io/import_ndjson.py and docs/scale-envelope.md establish source_id skip behavior, crash resumption, deferred push, and chunk-level commits. src/rebar/_cli/help/import.txt, the generated CLI reference, and docs/import-export.md retain pre-batching claims.\\n- Jira project selection. src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/access_check.py, runtime.py, and src/rebar/_bridge_runner.py require a configured project for access, inbound scope, and writes. docs/config.md, docs/jira-sync-setup.md, bridge-probe help, and generated CLI help describe a DIG fallback or call the project optional.\\n- Jira onboarding. src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py and ADR 0070 establish rebar bridge setup. scripts/jira-onboarding-reference/README.md calls the flow planned.\\n- Jira pressure tools. Both maintained pressure scripts default REBAR_TICKET_CLI to deleted src/rebar/_engine/rebar. Their README therefore describes commands that cannot start from the current checkout.\\n- Identity propagation. Four maintained workflows export REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY through GITHUB_ENV for later steps. docs/identity-setup.md says that channel does not reach later steps.\\n- CLI syntax. src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/writes.py accepts a positional parent and --detected-by for create. src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/lifecycle.py accepts --caused-by, --ref, and structured output for transition. The committed help omits part of those surfaces.\\n- MCP summaries. docs/mcp-reference.md truncates create_identity, create_ticket, link_tickets, log_session, reopen_ticket, set_file_impact, and transition_ticket at hard line breaks in registrar docstrings. The transition registrar also describes a narrower close contract than the CLI and core.\\n- Effective Gerrit gate state. infra/gerrit/project.config contains an active Verified submit requirement. infra/runbooks/two-vote-gate-rollback.md says the requirement ships inactive.\\n- GitHub mirror capabilities. SUPPORT.md uses GitHub Issues and the Verified gate uses GitHub Actions. infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md instructs operators to disable both.\\n- SSO operations. infra/terraform/modules/sso-gate/README.md links to missing infra/shared/auth/RUNBOOK.md. The maintained runbook is infra/runbooks/sso-auth-host.md.\\n- ADR lifecycle. ADR 0042 and ADR 0090 declare Accepted after explicit supersession notices. scripts/check_adr_numbers.py checks numbering, markers, and links only.\\n- Internal architecture. docs/architecture.md includes unimplemented ADR 0098 and ADR 0100 designs as architecture sections, plus completed module-split histories. docs/concurrency.md and docs/event-schema.md name retired shell writers.\\n- Obsolete plans. docs/oss-comparison-and-remediation.md and docs/remediation-implementation-plan.md retain absent-feature claims for capabilities now present in source.\\n- Module policy. docs/maintenance-audit-runbook.md calls 800 lines a soft cap. .github/module-size-limit.txt and AGENTS.md define an absolute cap.\\n- Public library documentation. unlink, tag, untag, archive, and compact are exported from src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py without function docstrings.\\n- Prompt inventory. tests/unit/test_reviewer_prompt_hygiene.py says the glob covers 41 reviewer prompts. The current glob resolves 58 files.\\n- Generated and synchronized surfaces. docs/adr/README.md is generated, templates/AGENTS.md contains a synchronized canonical region, and CLI help files have a generator. The current generated-surface table does not catalog every such surface.\\n- Link scope. scripts/check_docs_index.py validates relative links under docs. It does not cover the broken internal link found under infra.\\n- Third-party material. pyproject.toml lists only LICENSE in license-files. The v2 alias wordlist cites docs/licenses/adjective-adjective-animal-LICENSE.txt. The legacy wordlist lacks provenance. The Jira Data Center Dockerfile names an upstream path without an upstream revision or license.\\n- Skill metadata. examples/agent-skills/rebar-brainstorm/SKILL.md lacks the name field required by examples/agent-skills/README.md.\\n- Help discovery. Top-level help omits six routed command families identified in the prior checkpoint. Open RP-05 tickets loony-fabric-bunny and pettish-snippy-rasbora own the registry and generated-reference cutover.\\n\\nThis map records expected behavior sources rather than scan-count inference. No project files changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787291364519298001,"uuid":"5dcccc90-aba3-466d-8508-84c538d917aa"}